From: Zone Launcher
Subject: [PATCH] Unload the level when the window is closed

Closing the game window makes SDL request quit on the same frame the
deferred KERNEL:disconnect is queued, so CApplication::Run exits before
the level is unloaded. The render light DB then still holds lights at
exit; their destructors lock the spatial DB that was freed together with
g_pGamePersistent, and the process hangs forever in static destructors.

---
diff --git a/src/xrEngine/x_ray.cpp b/src/xrEngine/x_ray.cpp
index 20d2e576e..69d6602d7 100644
--- a/src/xrEngine/x_ray.cpp
+++ b/src/xrEngine/x_ray.cpp
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include "xrCore/Threading/TaskManager.hpp"
 #include "xrNetServer/NET_AuthCheck.h"
 
+#include "IGame_Level.h"
 #include "IGame_Persistent.h"
 #include "LightAnimLibrary.h"
 #include "XR_IOConsole.h"
@@ -436,6 +437,18 @@ int CApplication::Run()
         FrameMarkEnd(FRAME_MARK_APPLICATION_RUN);
     } // while (!SDL_QuitRequested())
 
+    // Closing the window makes SDL request quit on the same frame the deferred
+    // KERNEL:disconnect is queued, so the loop exits before the level is unloaded.
+    // Its lights would then outlive g_pGamePersistent's spatial DB and deadlock
+    // in static destructors on exit. Unload it now; the pending quit keeps the
+    // disconnect handler from reopening the main menu.
+    if (g_pGameLevel)
+    {
+        if (!Engine.Event.Peek("KERNEL:quit"))
+            Engine.Event.Defer("KERNEL:quit");
+        Engine.Event.Signal("KERNEL:disconnect");
+    }
+
     Device.Shutdown();
 
     return 0;
